<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Wield</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> wield &lt;weapon&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre> wield long sword
</pre>
<p>To start using a weapon, you must use the 'wield' command. If the weapon
is two-handed, you must have both hands free, else, your weapon hand must
be free. Whether a weapon takes one hand or two is decided by its kind:
you can't choose to wield a one-handed weapon in two hands. A shield, or
something you hold, takes up a hand too. When you wield a weapon, you are
told how good you are at fighting with it.
</p><p>A weapon that is too big or too small for you can't be wielded (see
<a cmd='#'>Help Resize</a>).
</p><p>To wield two weapons, you must hold the second weapon using the <a cmd='#'>Hold|Help Hold</a> command.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre> &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Hold</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>
 &gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Remove</a>
</pre>




</div>